Description: scaleplex_inlineass: buffer pre-graph sub chunks (Phase 2b)
 Phase 2 (patch 0100) wired -map_inlineass through fftools. End-to-end
 worked when the subtitle stream lives in the SAME input as the video
 (PMS argv shape `-i source.mkv -map_inlineass 0:s:N`), because the
 demuxer emits a single packet stream and configure_filtergraph runs
 before the first sub packet flows.
 .
 It did NOT work when the subtitle stream is on a SEPARATE input
 (`-i source.mkv -i temp-0.srt -map_inlineass 1:s:0`), because
 jellyfin-ffmpeg 7.x's scheduler decodes the (tiny, instantly-EOF)
 SRT input ahead of the video graph's first frame. handle_subtitle
 fires twice with dec_ctx already valid, but every binding has
 flt_ctx == NULL because configure_filtergraph hasn't run yet; the
 sub packets pass through with no append target and are lost. By the
 time the video filter graph configures and link_graph populates
 flt_ctx, there are no more subs to feed.
 .
 This patch fixes the race by:
 .
   1. Adding a per-binding pending-chunk queue. handle_subtitle
      decomposes the AVSubtitle into (start_ms, duration_ms, ass_line)
      tuples and either replays them into vf_inlineass immediately
      (binding has flt_ctx) or buffers them (binding still pre-graph).
      Buffer is capped at INLINEASS_PENDING_MAX (4096) per binding to
      avoid runaway; over-cap chunks log once and are dropped.
 .
   2. Adding eager-bind in handle_subtitle. If no binding currently
      pins dec_ctx, look it up via ist->decoder; on match, pin
      b->dec_ctx and accept the chunk. Lets the buffer accumulate
      even before link_graph runs.
 .
   3. Adding scaleplex_inlineass_link_graph drain. After flt_ctx is
      set and font/storage-size pushed, flush the buffered chunks via
      a new public side-channel helper avfilter_inlineass_replay_chunk.
      The helper bypasses AVSubtitle reconstruction (we already have
      ASS_TIME_BASE-ready tuples) but otherwise behaves like
      avfilter_inlineass_append_data: takes the same global libass
      lock, calls process_header on first chunk if needed, then
      ass_process_chunk per line.
 .
   4. Unifying the immediate path: handle_subtitle now also uses
      avfilter_inlineass_replay_chunk for in-graph dispatch (instead
      of reconstructing an AVSubtitle for avfilter_inlineass_append_data).
      Single code path for buffered + immediate.
 .
 Re-bind on probe→live configure_filtergraph re-entry also calls
 pending_free on each binding — anything queued for the now-defunct
 graph is dropped (its flt_ctx is being freed); the live graph will
 see fresh subs as decoding resumes.
 .
 Cap rationale: 2-hour movie at 3 subs/sec upper bound = ~22k chunks.
 The pre-graph window is bounded by how long configure_filtergraph
 takes (usually one video probe cycle, <2 s of clock time → <60 sub
 chunks at typical rates). 4096 covers any realistic backlog with a
 wide safety margin; beyond that we're either pathological or a bug.
 .
 Worker rewriter cleanup deferred to a follow-up: with this patch
 ffmpeg handles both embedded and sidecar -map_inlineass argv
 natively, so the rewriter's findSidecarSubtitle, subtitle_extract.go,
 hybrid-inlineass swap mode, and HLS+seek PTS-shift bracket can all
 be deleted — leaving only a small regex strip for the 4 Plex-only
 filter keys (:language=, :overrides=, :outline=, :shadow=).
Origin: scaleplex (no Plex equivalent — Plex 6.x's single-threaded
        transcode never exposed this ordering bug)
Forwarded: not-needed
Author: scaleplex
Last-Update: 2026-05-12
